    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy is delighted to present this wonderful three-bedroom detached red-brick bungalow to the market. Uniquely set back from the road on a generous plot of approximately 0.2 acres, this charming property has been lovingly maintained by its owners over the years. Positioned along the highly desirable Skerries Road, the home combines peaceful semi-rural surroundings with quick, convenient access to Lusk Village, coastal Skerries, and excellent commuting infrastructure.\n\nPassing through the entrance porch, the home opens into a warm reception hallway that leads to the light-filled accommodation. It offers excellent flow across a single level, featuring dual reception space, a bright front living room and an adjacent family room. Perfect for formal entertaining or daily relaxation. Toward the rear, a spacious open-plan kitchen and dining area forms the heart of the home. The sleeping quarters comprise three well-proportioned bedrooms, supported by two bathrooms, ensuring practical convenience for family living and guests alike.Externally the property features a manicured lawn framed by mature hedging and a long driveway providing ample off-street parking. The driveway leads down the side to a solid detached garage, offering secure parking, workshop space, or valuable storage. Beyond the garage, the private rear garden backs directly onto peaceful open countryside, providing a serene backdrop alongside incredible scope for future home extensions (subject to planning permission).\n\nThe location is second to none, enviably positioned between Lusk Village and the coastal town of Skerries. Residents enjoy immediate proximity to local primary and secondary schools, supermarkets, and sports clubs, while the beaches, harbour, and dining options of Skerries are just minutes away. Commuters benefit from swift transport links, with Rush & Lusk Train Station nearby alongside regular bus routes and easy access to the M1, M50, and Dublin Airport. This property represents a rare opportunity to acquire a character-filled detached residence on a substantial site in one of North County Dublin's most sought-after addresses."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Gas Fired Central Heating</li><li> Septic Tank</li><li> Approx. 0.2 Acres</li><li> Detached Red-Brick Bungalow</li><li> Set on c. 0.2 acres.</li><li> Two reception rooms</li><li> Lovingly Maintained throughout.</li><li> Detached Garage offering ideal workshop space, storage, or conversion potential</li><li> Expansive Front & Rear Grounds backing onto peaceful open countryside views</li><li> Ample Off-Street Parking</li><li> Immense Extension Potential to the side or rear (SPP).</li><li> Excellent Location on Skerries Road within minutes of Lusk Village, Skerries town, beaches, and Rush & Lusk Train Station.</ul>"
      },
